# synth-optimizers changelog

## 2026-06-09

* Prepared `0.2.1.dev202606092146` for hosted optimizer SDK/CLI launch-readiness; no PyPI publish yet.
* Added hosted GELO public authoring APIs: `GeloHostedConfig`, typed sections, `GeloPreset`, and `GeloMaterializer`.
* Added hosted GELO CLI paths: `gelo startup`, `gelo materialize`, `gelo submit`, `gelo watch`, and bundled `gelo console` docs.
* Moved GEPA hosted submit/watch onto `HostedOptimizerClient`, including SynthTunnel and pool submit support.
* Added strict hosted client parsing for startup catalogs, run statuses, billing feature readiness, NDJSON, and SSE payloads.
* Added `HostedOptimizerClient.event_backfill()` for finite lifecycle event proof; streaming `events()` remains for monitoring.
* Made hosted client artifact, lifecycle event backfill, and Go-Ex event backfill errors name the failing surface.
* Made GELO public config materialization reject retired proposer backend aliases instead of remapping them silently.
* Made hosted CLI help/startup import without eager GEPA local runtime dependencies; GEPA symbols now fail loudly only when used.
* Added public hosted GEPA/GELO docs and linked them from the package README.
* Added the `banking77` optional extra for repeatable hosted GEPA proof dependencies.
* Blocked release items remain: staging/live hosted proofs, positive-cost billing evidence or waiver, deploy-target proof, and no-secret log review.

## 2026-06-04

* Started the `0.2.1.dev` cycle (post-release dev).
* Added a paid NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra proposer via OpenRouter (`nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b`, no `:free`) through the proven Codex+Responses path; added a provider-agnostic `chat_completions` proposer backend for NVIDIA-direct (Codex no longer supports the chat wire).
* Published `0.2.0.20260604` to PyPI (first non-dev daily release; pins `synth-containers==0.2.0.20260604`).
* Added `gepa console`: the run board and the bundled GEPA docs served behind one local port as `Board` | `Docs` tabs (click or `1`/`2`/`T` to switch).
* Shipped GEPA docs (CLI, SDK, algorithms, containers) as package data under `synth_optimizers/docs/gepa`, served by the console with no repo checkout.
* Extracted the shared board route/SSE handler so the board and console serve one implementation.
* Fixed acceptance config generation to emit `task_pools` under `[gepa]` (standalone `GepaRun.from_toml` rejects `[taskset.task_pools]`).
* Unified the GEPA task-pools location: the service request now takes `task_pools` as a top-level field (sibling of `taskset`), matching the SDK `GepaConfig` and the standalone `[gepa.task_pools]` TOML.
* Validated that task-pool ids are split-local — pareto/minibatch/reflection must come from `taskset.train_ids` and heldout from `taskset.heldout_ids` (fails at config time instead of mis-selecting at rollout).
* Typed the forecast confidence band in the limit engine so the interval multipliers match exhaustively (no silent zero-width interval), and dropped a fabricated total-token reservation fallback.

## 2026-06-02

* Published `0.2.0.dev202606021646` to PyPI.
* Added FlashEvolve async pipeline mode with reflective staleness reviewer.
* Fixed FlashEvolve async rollout folding to resolve rows by `example_id`.
* Documented the current FlashEvolve wall-clock regression vs `sync_serial` pending proposer-priority scheduling.

## 2026-05-31

* Published `0.2.0.dev202606010003` to PyPI with GEPA rollout resilience.
* Published `0.2.0.dev202605312141` to PyPI.
* Added typed 429 and container HTTP status handling for rollout failures.
* Added degraded rollout accounting, failure-rate breaker events, and terminal job retries.
* Added adaptive rollout concurrency backoff for provider overload.
* Pinned the matching daily-dev `synth-containers` package for clean wheel installs.
* Added typed GEPA SDK entrypoint: `OptimizerRun(GepaConfig(...)).execute()`.
* Added URL-only `synth-containers` handoff via `ContainerConnection`.
* Added container discovery for `program`, `objectives`, and `policy`.
* Added multi-objective GEPA selection, protected objectives, and ASI evidence.
* Added proposer prompt overrides and shipped best-practices export.
* Added OpenAI, OpenRouter, and ChatGPT proposer auth modes.
* Moved Codex auth, JSON-RPC, and usage normalization into platform agent runtime.
* Added live terminal policy/proposer usage rollups.
* Added direct DeepSeek V4 Flash proposer support for Banking77 GEPA: [PR #4](https://github.com/synth-laboratories/optimizers/pull/4).
* Merged [PR #3](https://github.com/synth-laboratories/optimizers/pull/3) `better-ai-auth`; [PR #2](https://github.com/synth-laboratories/optimizers/pull/2) remains the SDK base.

## 2026-05-30

* No main-branch package release.
* Better SDK and auth work stayed staged off main.
* Next release target: shorter SDK examples, acceptance evidence, and daily dev packaging.
